# Lets the user at the seat read a tablet's input nodes, which Sara's pen
# module reads the pen's buttons from, so the upper barrel button let go in the
# air is heard under Wayland. `uaccess` grants the active session's user alone,
# and only these nodes. Joining the input group would give every program that
# user runs every input device, the keyboard among them. The number is under
# 73, where systemd's seat rules apply the tag.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ENV{ID_INPUT_TABLET}=="1", TAG+="uaccess"
